From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:19:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter: add dovi_reshape filter

Apply the Dolby Vision RPU of each frame on the CPU and output PQ
BT.2020 RGB, so that profile 5 content can go through zscale and
tonemap without libplacebo:

  dovi_reshape,zscale=t=linear:npl=100,tonemap=hable,zscale=...

The filter takes planar YUV at 8 to 12 bits, upsamples chroma
bilinearly at the frame's chroma location (left when unspecified), and
reshapes and decodes each pixel with the shared helper. Output is
gbrpf32, full range. The Dolby Vision side data is removed; mastering
display metadata is rebuilt from the RPU's source luminance range, as
libplacebo does, and a level 1 block becomes the frame's content light
level. Frames without an RPU, limited range frames and residual
enhancement layers are refused.

The reshaped output matches vf_libplacebo's own reshaping to within one
10-bit PQ code value at the 95th percentile on a generated profile 5
clip.

The test runs the filter in a graph on a frame whose chroma is a ramp,
so every expected pixel is exact, and checks the side data. Two planted
cases, a wrong chroma siting and a wrong coefficient in the frame's RPU,
must miss the expected colours; a limited range frame must be refused.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
