diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 3534c87c9be9374db14189a28324cf95efc4b576..1c29a51458b99c37b541946dc15497d47028e9ac 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -12308,6 +12308,43 @@ please use tools/python/tf_sess_config.py to get the configs of TensorFlow backe
 
 @end itemize
 
+@section dovi_reshape
+Apply the Dolby Vision reshaping signalled in each frame's RPU and decode the
+result to nonlinear (PQ) BT.2020 RGB.
+
+Single-layer Dolby Vision streams such as profile 5 carry their picture in a
+proprietary IPT colour space that only the RPU metadata turns into displayable
+colour. This filter performs that step on the CPU, so that @ref{zscale} and
+@ref{tonemap} can process the output like HDR10 content. The math follows the
+Dolby Vision support in libplacebo.
+
+The input is planar YUV with 8 to 12 bits per component, full range, with
+@code{AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_METADATA} side data on every frame, as the HEVC and AV1
+decoders export it. Chroma is upsampled bilinearly, honouring the frame's chroma
+location. The output is @code{gbrpf32} tagged as BT.2020 primaries, SMPTE ST 2084
+transfer and full range. The Dolby Vision side data is removed, and mastering
+display metadata built from the RPU's source luminance range replaces any the
+frame carried. When the RPU has a level 1 block, its maximum and average
+luminance of the shot become the frame's content light level (MaxCLL and
+MaxFALL); without one, content light level metadata is removed.
+
+In addition, the 12-bit PQ code values (0 to 4095) from the level 1 block are
+exported as frame metadata keys @code{lavfi.dovi.l1_max_pq} and
+@code{lavfi.dovi.l1_avg_pq}, corresponding to the shot's maximum and average PQ
+luminance. When a frame has no level 1 block, both keys are removed from the
+frame metadata.
+
+Frames without Dolby Vision metadata, limited range frames, and streams whose RPU
+signals a residual enhancement layer (profile 7) are refused with an error.
+
+The filter has no options.
+
+@subsection Example
+Tone map a profile 5 file to SDR BT.709:
+@example
+ffmpeg -i dv5.mp4 -vf dovi_reshape,zscale=t=linear:npl=100,tonemap=hable:desat=0,zscale=p=bt709:t=bt709:m=bt709:r=tv,format=yuv420p out.mp4
+@end example
+
 @section drawbox
 
 Draw a colored box on the input image.
